'''Larry Jack Mildren''' (October 10, 1949 – May 22, 2008), was an American [[American football|football]] player and politician. He was an [[1971 College Football All-America Team|All-American]] [[quarterback]] at the [[Oklahoma Sooners football|University of Oklahoma]], and professional football player with the [[1972 Baltimore Colts season|Baltimore Colts]] and [[1974 New England Patriots season|New England Patriots]]. A native Texan, he was later an oil company owner, elected as the 13th [[lieutenant governor of Oklahoma]], and enjoyed a career as a successful bank executive in [[Oklahoma]].

